{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 8570,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video is sponsored by Caseta by Lutron"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17480,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to the general theory of relativity, gravity is not a force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22000,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are no gravitational fields, gravity is kind of an illusion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27820,
    "dDurationMs": 8400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in this video, I will prove it to you by blasting off into outer space in 321"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50050,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Albert Einstein said the happiest thought of his life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53820,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was imagining a man falling off the roof of a house."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58740,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What made Einstein so happy about this wasn't Schadenfreude,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63080,
    "dDurationMs": 5430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was the realization that this man, while he was falling wouldn't feel his own weight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68510,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He would be weightless and anything he dropped on his way down,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72220,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, it would remain stationary relative to him or moving in uniform motion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78050,
    "dDurationMs": 5090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The whole situation would be just like.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83140,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you were in deep space, not near any large masses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88850,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With your spaceship at rest or coasting along at constant velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94220,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, you would feel no weight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97370,
    "dDurationMs": 8570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Objects would remain stationary relative to you or if you give them a push, they would move in a straight line at constant velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105940,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you would be the very definition of an inertial observer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110510,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're not accelerating, not in a gravitational field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114060,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the laws of physics apply in your reference frame,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117540,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning there is no experiment, you could do to distinguish your initial reference frame from any other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127020,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now here comes the big leap:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129020,
    "dDurationMs": 6060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Einstein looks at these two scenarios and says they are equivalent, not just similar"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135080,
    "dDurationMs": 2630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Physically, they are exactly the same thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137710,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which means man falling from roof is not in a gravitational field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141600,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are no gravitational fields, and he is not accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145540,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He is an inertial observer, just like Rocket Man."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149250,
    "dDurationMs": 6460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whoa, whoa, whoa. I mean, okay, I can see how both of these observers feel weightless."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155710,
    "dDurationMs": 3490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But man falling from roof is clearly in a gravitational field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159200,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, he's right next to the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161250,
    "dDurationMs": 5530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he's obviously accelerating his speed is increasing by 9.8 meters per second, every second"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166780,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A fact that will become painfully apparent when he crashes into the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171400,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know that these two situations look very different,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175020,
    "dDurationMs": 5980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but Einstein's equivalence principle tells us the one thing to focus on: the experience of the observer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181400,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If they feel weightless than they are in an inertial frame of reference"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185680,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every bit as good as rocket man's out drifting through deep space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189880,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine if Rocket Man coasting along at constant velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193320,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " and not paying attention comes upon a planet a long way off in the distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204680,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An external observer might notice that the path of the rocket bends ever so slightly towards the planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210320,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But inside, Rocket Man would remain oblivious."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214100,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He feels no force, experiences no acceleration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218000,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As the rocket gets closer to the planet, it goes faster and faster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221620,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Rocket Man still feels weightless. For him, nothing has changed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226420,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So where on this journey would you say the frame of reference changes from inertial to non inertial?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230920,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An onboard accelerometer would never even register a blip."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234840,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He has continued on his inertial path through spacetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239100,
    "dDurationMs": 6260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the logical conclusion is his frame of reference is inertial up until the instant he crashes into the planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251840,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so how do you explain the curved path of his rocket without gravitational forces or gravitational fields?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258360,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer is curved spacetime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261440,
    "dDurationMs": 7140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First focus on rocket man's observation that the whole time he felt like he was moving with constant velocity in a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269180,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was moving in a straight line through spacetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272420,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but space time around massive objects, like planets is curved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276240,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that's why his path appeared curved to a distant observer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281200,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now this isn't as unusual as it seems,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283680,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Airplanes, for example, always try to fly the shortest route between cities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287720,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Essentially, they just go in a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290060,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But since the Earth's surface is curved, the shortest path doesn't look like a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295280,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These shortest paths over curved surfaces are called geodesics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299240,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we use that same word, geodesics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302100,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the straight line paths followed by inertial observers through curved space time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306900,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's another analogy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308600,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine you and a friend are standing 1000 kilometers apart on the equator."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313780,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now you both set off due North."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316060,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over time you will come closer together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318460,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately bumping into each other at the North Pole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321320,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s as though there was a force pushing you together, but you didn't feel a force and your friend didn't feel a force.\\N"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328680,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravity is just like that force, it doesn't actually exist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333840,
    "dDurationMs": 6780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The real reason for you coming together was that you were both on straight paths, geodesics, on a curved surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342940,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Astronauts on the space station are weightless."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346020,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means they too are inertial observers traveling on a geodesic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350980,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the earth curves space time around it, which is why their straight line path appears as a helix."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358180,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It only looks like a circular orbit if you forget the time dimension."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362540,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Don't forget, we are all moving through space and time, spacetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369840,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the standard bent sheet analogy for curved space time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374680,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I think this demo is misleading."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376900,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It allows you to fool yourself into thinking you understand general relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380820,
    "dDurationMs": 8620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when the intuition you're actually drawing on is just that objects like to fall towards the middle of a well due to the gravitational force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390060,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in general relativity, there is no gravitational force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393740,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you should be thinking about is objects traveling on a straight line path through spacetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399060,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It just so happens that spacetime is curved around massive objects,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403440,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that straight line path doesn't look like a straight line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408140,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Matter tells spacetime how to curve, and spacetime tells matter how to move."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416780,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now let's go back to deep space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419700,
    "dDurationMs": 6660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What happens if you turn on the rocket thrusters and accelerate at 9.8 meters per second squared?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427700,
    "dDurationMs": 7920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, someone outside would see all objects remain stationary, while the floor of the rocket accelerates into them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442280,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Inside the rocket, everything would appear to accelerate down to the ground"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447100,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you would feel a force pushing up on your feet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450580,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same force that's pushing up on you as you watch this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456200,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This situation feels exactly the same as being at rest on the surface of Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465780,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cause we are at rest on the surface of Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469120,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want to ask you, are you watching this video in an inertial frame of reference?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474660,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I mean, do you feel weightless?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477640,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, so you are not an inertial observer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481220,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your situation is exactly the same as someone accelerating on a rocket ship in deep space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486520,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And let me be clear,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487540,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't mean the being at rest and a gravitational field is like accelerating and a rocket."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492440,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, it is the exact same thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495020,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are accelerating and there is no gravitational field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498620,
    "dDurationMs": 1820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravitational fields do not exist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500960,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I know that sounds crazy, but come with me for a minute."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513280,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514860,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in standard Newtonian physics we draw your weight force, the force of gravity pushing you down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521660,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the normal force from the floor pushing you up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525040,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We say these forces are equal and opposite, so there's no net force on you, so you are not accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530960,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in general relativity, gravity is not a force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535540,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have no weight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537560,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the only force on you are these normal forces pushing you up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541720,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you are accelerating upwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544000,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I'm not moving up!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546200,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Relative to what?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547760,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, relative to the flip chart and the floor and basically everything in this room."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551620,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But all of those things are in your frame of reference, which you know is not inertial."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556720,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Relative to everything in my rocket ship, I'm not accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562680,
    "dDurationMs": 6100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you need if you really want to measure your acceleration is someone in an inertial frame of reference,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568780,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the guy who fell off the roof"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571320,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he would see you accelerating up at 9.8 meters per second squared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577800,
    "dDurationMs": 7460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think what this shows is that what an acceleration really is is it's a deviation from a geodesic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586080,
    "dDurationMs": 6380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can't follow a straight line path through space time because the floor prevents you from doing that:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592460,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it applies a force upwards on you, so you're accelerating up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596560,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if I'm accelerating up and so is everyone else around the world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600740,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and presumably the whole surface of the Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603120,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, shouldn't the earth be expanding?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606140,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No. It is possible for you to be accelerating, even though your spatial coordinates are not changing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613260,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I will show you one equation from general relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617340,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This says that the second derivative of your position with respect to time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622040,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to your acceleration, that's just f on m,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626320,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you were in flat spacetime, well, this is exactly what you're saying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630680,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you're accelerating your spatial coordinates have to change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633840,
    "dDurationMs": 6540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you're not in flat space time, and this term is related to the curvature of spacetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640380,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " and this is your velocity through time squared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644320,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You don't have to worry about the details here, the point is your position can be not changing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650400,
    "dDurationMs": 7060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This can be zero, which means your acceleration must be exactly equal to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657460,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this curvature term times are velocity through time squared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662300,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in curved spacetime, you need to accelerate just to stand still."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670340,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot of this may seem more complicated than Newtonian physics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673900,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but one classical mystery looks a whole lot simpler in general relativity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679000,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is why all objects fall at the same rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685100,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I have made a number of videos on this topic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687680,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I would always give the standard Newtonian explanation:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691120,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the only force on a free falling body is its weight g m m on r squared,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695440,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which equals its mass times acceleration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698000,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can cancel the objects mass on both sides of the equation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 701380,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hence, all objects will have this same acceleration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 705600,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The mystery is why we could cancel these two m's,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709820,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the one on the left was gravitational mass, the property of an object that creates and experiences a gravitational field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716540,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While the m on the right is inertial mass, a measure of resistance to acceleration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722620,
    "dDurationMs": 5860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why should these two conceptually different properties be numerically identical?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729440,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists have spent a lot of time and effort experimentally testing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733260,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down to around one part in 10 trillion that these two types of mass really are the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740220,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in general relativity, there is no mystery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743820,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All objects appear to fall the same way because they're not accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748220,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're just following straight line pass through spacetime until they encounter something that stops them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753440,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like the objects in the rocket ship, they appear to accelerate at the same rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757740,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they're not really accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759980,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the floor accelerating into them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764280,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, a lot of us might seem pretty far fetched "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766580,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as it did back in 1915 when Einstein proposed it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769980,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So he very cleverly came up with a measurable prediction that scientists could make to test his theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775920,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine that this rocket ship is coasting through deep space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780140,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you shine a light beam across the rocket ship, well it'll do exactly what you expect:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 785460,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light travels in a straight line and hits a point on the opposite wall at exactly the same height as the source."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792020,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now what if this rocket is accelerating?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795160,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, to an external observer, they're still going to see the same thing: light traveling in a straight line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801100,
    "dDurationMs": 7560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but inside the rocket, during the time it takes the light to travel across the cabin, The rocket will have sped up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808660,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So by the time it hits the other wall, it'll hit a little lower than before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814240,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in an accelerating frame of reference light deflects down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820740,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here I'm dramatically exaggerating the effect,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even if I were accelerating up at 10 G's, which would probably kill me,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828320,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the deflection would be on the order of the width of a proton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832500,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still, it shows that an accelerating frame of reference will bend light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838300,
    "dDurationMs": 5740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Einstein reasoned light must also bend when it passes a large mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844040,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But where do you find a mass large enough?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846860,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the only obvious huge mass near the Earth is the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852100,
    "dDurationMs": 7240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the ideal experiment would be to look at light passing just next to the sun and see if it is deflected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859340,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Say light from distant stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862220,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem was, of course, the sun is just so bright, you can't see stars right next to it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867060,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unless there is a total solar eclipse, which is exactly what happened in 1919"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873020,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Arthur Eddington set out to take pictures of the stars right next to the sun during totality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880940,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what he found by analyzing those pictures,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883480,
    "dDurationMs": 8100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was that their positions appeared deflected by the precise amount predicted by Einstein's general theory of relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891580,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The result was twice the deflection some had calculated using a strictly Newtonian model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896700,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And general relativity has passed virtually every test put to it over the past hundred years or so,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902120,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there are still more things to try"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909520,
    "dDurationMs": 7820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A well known and empirically validated finding is that accelerating charges radiates electromagnetic radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917340,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So one conceptually simple experimental test"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920540,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be to compare the behavior of a stationary charge and a gravitational field to a free falling one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927040,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If a more Newtonian picture of gravity is correct,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930500,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well then the stationary charge should not radiate electromagnetic radiation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934660,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a free falling one is accelerating and therefore it should radiate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939080,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, general relativity sees the free-falling charge as non accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944800,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just going on a straight line path through curve space time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948080,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whereas the stationary charge is accelerating and therefore it should give off electromagnetic radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955320,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, thus far logistical challenges have prevented anyone from actually carrying out this experiment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960540,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but what you believe will happen reveals what you truly think about the nature of gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 967820,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you think that a freely falling charge will radiate electromagnetic radiation or not?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974400,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is gravity an illusion?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979920,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This episode was sponsored by Caseta"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981960,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so I used the sponsorship money to have a rocket ship built"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990340,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Caseta by Lutron makes these smart light switches in the rocket ship."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993760,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They also make remotes, motion sensors, smart plugs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basically every smart switch you could use for turning things in your home on and off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001880,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But installing a smart switch isn't rocket science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005140,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You just turn off the power to the switch, detach the existing wires,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008840,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and reconnect them to the Caseta smart switch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011460,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's great about smart switches, as opposed to smart bulbs, is one switch often controls multiple bulbs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1017980,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can save money by replacing only the switch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020880,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they connect to most smart devices like Alexa, Google Assistant, and Apple home kit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026540,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you can control them via an app on your phone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029520,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you forget to turn off the lights and the rocket, no need to go back, just turn them off in the app."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035600,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can also use the app to set up schedules, turning the lights on when it goes dark."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040280,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This gives you peace of mind knowing your family will always come home to a well lit house."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045200,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we may not have personal rockets yet, but we have smart switches"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049140,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the smart choice for these devices is Caseta by Lutron."
    } ]
  } ]
}
